  "id": "Compound::DB00960 - Disease::DOID:10763",
  "verbalization": "Pindolol is closely related to other beta-blockers through a shared structural similarity, which places it within the broader class of Beta-Adrenergic Antagonists. This structural similarity links Pindolol to Alprenolol and Penbutolol, both of which are known to treat hypertension. The evidence suggests that Pindolol, through its resemblance to these compounds, may share similar pharmacological effects, potentially contributing to its ability to lower blood pressure. The commonality of the Beta-Adrenergic Antagonist class and the treatment of hypertension by its members implies a potential mechanism of action that involves modulating adrenergic signaling, which is a well-established pathway in blood pressure regulation. The integration of these relationships highlights the importance of structural similarity in drug repurposing, where molecular likeness can predict therapeutic outcomes.",
